From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 09:07:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] pco: instruction selection, scheduling, control flow and
 RA improvements

Improvements to the PowerVR Compiler Optimiser in four groups; each was
developed and measured separately.

Instruction selection and folding
  - fold single-use imul into iadd, and single-use fmad/fmul/fadd into fsat
  - translate ffract natively as a single fmad
  - fold a phase 0 ALU op into a following min/max group
  - fuse "op (b << n)" into a single bitwise group
  - lower imprecise fdot4 as two parallel mul + fma chains
  - fold constant trailing channels of 8-bit UNORM pixel outputs
  - swap commutative sources rather than inserting a mov
  - skip the NaN expansion of fmin/fmax when one operand is a constant

Scheduling and dual issue
  - co-issue independent ALU ops in phases 0 and 1
  - schedule for dual issue before register allocation
  - drop moves around push constants, bitfield ops and shifted adds
  - restore back-propagation of pixel output writes, without doing so into
    source-encoded destinations

Control flow
  - branch over uniform if bodies and compare straight into p0
  - lower loops that every instance runs alike to plain branches
  - keep the execution condition of instructions replaced after CF lowering
  - skip empty blocks when stepping between instruction groups
  - ignore the other branch of a uniform if for DITR pre-fences
  - raise the unroll threshold (16 -> 128 iterations)

Register allocation
  - keep a register first written inside a loop live across it
  - propagate register reads into their uses
  - hoist repeated immediates into a register within a block
  - load 32-bit literals from a shared register pool
  - preload up to 256 dwords of uniform buffer data
  - shrink vecs that have collated sources

Also fixes 16-bit flrp and 16-bit float conversions, resolves pixel-rate vs
sample-rate at compile time when it is known, skips the compute instance
check
for whole-task workgroups, tests only the address word of a texture state
for
null, and reads pixel coordinates directly in single-sampled transfer
shaders.

Measurements (three shader-heavy probes, each with its control probe):

  probe      unit     before      after      gain     vs vendor
  vkheavy    ms       858.5       255.8      3.36x    4.77x -> 1.42x
  cstpi      M/s      26.6        72.8       2.74x    5.53x -> 2.02x
  cstpf      M/s      29.6        87.9       2.97x    4.93x -> 1.66x

The control probe (cstpin, the register-operand form of cstpi) does not
move,
which makes the gains attributable to these changes rather than to the
machine:
hoisting should make the immediate form cost what the register form costs,
and
it now does (cstpi 72.8 vs cstpin 71.3).

Correctness: glmark2-es2 --validate reports 27 scenes validated OK, and the
Vulkan render tests pass at 512 (262144/262144) and 2048 (4194304/4194304).

The driver-side changes that enable some of these (pco options passed from
the
pipeline, pooled literal setup, descriptor checks recorded at draw time)
are
deliberately not in this series.

